koppel (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixes a gap in the UI's access rules: a request with a gRPC content type
    skipped the check of KOPPEL_UI_ALLOW_FROM.
  * The UI keeps sessions in memory, so everyone signs in again once. On Linux
    and in Docker the first password needs the setup token from the log
    (journalctl -u koppel).
  * Koppel machines talk Skakel protocol 3: a 0.2.1 machine does not link with
    a 0.2.0 one, so update both ends. The first start rewrites secrets.json and
    there is no way back, so back up /var/lib/koppel first.
  * Settings are KOPPEL_* variables and --options; the 0.1.x names still work
    and are logged as deprecated. The key can be kept outside the data folder
    (KOPPEL_KEY_FILE or the koppel-key systemd credential).
  * An upgrade no longer enables a unit the administrator disabled or
    restarts a stopped service. The full notes are in CHANGELOG.md in the
    repository.

 -- Matumi Software <70009674+RikusVanRensburg@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

koppel (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Koppel is rewritten in Rust, with the same web UI and features, small
    enough for a Raspberry Pi Zero.
  * The package comes for amd64, arm64 and armhf, needs no other package, and
    upgrades 0.1.x in place, keeping /var/lib/koppel.
  * systemd restarts a Koppel that hangs, and the service runs with systemd's
    sandbox.
  * There is no way back to 0.1.x, and Koppel machines talk Skakel protocol 2,
    so update every machine. The full notes are in CHANGELOG.md in the
    repository.

 -- Matumi Software <70009674+RikusVanRensburg@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
